      "abstract_full": "For every odd prime p, the Young module labelled by λ = (2p−2,1) in characteristic p is simple, whereas its corresponding polynomial injective hull I_n(λ) is nonprojective for every n≥2. At parameter q=1, this gives a negative answer to the unrestricted formulation of Miyachi’s Conjecture 7 in the 2009 Oberwolfach report. The proof combines classical representation theory with a labelled rank-truncation argument. We include explicit proofs of the local calculations and reproducible supporting checks. Historical priority remains unresolved; no firstness claim is made.",
      "title": "Simple Young modules with nonprojective polynomial injective hulls",
